  "unitNotes": {
    "crateKg": "Tomato crates in the Pune/Narayangaon trade are commonly 20 kg. Trade convention, not a statute — confirm with the team before relying on it.",
    "bagKg": "Onion, potato and grain bags (gonpat / pote / bori) are commonly 50 kg. Trade convention — confirm with the team.",
    "weatherSensitivity": "RK-4 scaling of the rain anomaly, 0–1: high for perishables harvested and sold wet (tomato, onion, grapes, chilli), low for stored grains. A design prior, not a measurement. It only scales one signal, and that signal's say in the evidence vote is its measured out-of-fold skill, so a wrong prior costs weight, not correctness."
